Items Requiring Business/Integration Confirmation
These are not classified as defects without the missing contract evidence:
• Window end key. The service ends its operating window at HORA_OP_CEP_FIN, the SPEI/CEP cut-off key shared with Email, Calypso_Liquidacion, and SPEI_CEP_GEN_CDA, while every other SWIFT outgoing service gates on HORA_OP_FIN (READ-FR-6). Provide the production values of both parameters.
• Message-type convention. The code prefixes MT- to MESSAGE_TYPE before comparing it with MT-998 (implying the field arrives without a prefix) and passes the raw field to the insert procedure, whose special case tests @cve_mensaje = 'MT-199'; the unit tests use both forms (MT-998, 998, and MT-199). Confirm what VW_T24_SWF_MESSAGES.MESSAGE_TYPE contains for an MT 199 (READ-FR-9, READ-FR-16, READ-FR-19).
• 998 routing and envelope. The C# builds a sender, a receiver BIC, and a full {1:...}{2:...}{3:...}{4:...} envelope for each 998 message, but the DAO persists only the folio, type, reference, and body, and the ETL resolves the destination from tb_bilun_mensajes_swift. Confirm that downstream routing by customer is intended and that the envelope fields are not needed (READ-FR-9).
• Insight column types and nullability. The query builds the SWIFT body by string concatenation and formats amounts with CAST(... AS VARCHAR). Confirm the types of CUSTOMER_ID, DRAWDOWN_NET_AMT, AMOUNT, TOT_INTEREST_AMT, INTEREST_RATE, and INTEREST_SPREAD, whether NAME_1, INTEREST_SPREAD, and the currency can be NULL, and how many clients are configured for mensaje = '998' (READ-FR-4, READ-FR-14).
• Work-table DDL. Confirm whether tb_srv_swf_trabajo.nf_mq_msg accepts NULL and which unique constraints guard (nf_folio, nf_tipo) and (folio, tipo_operacion); the insert procedure's check-then-insert is only safe under single-instance operation (READ-FR-4, READ-FR-16).
• T24 behavior for synthetic headers. The marking step submits an update for every processed folio, including the generated 998 folios that are not T24 DE.O.HEADER identifiers. T24 is expected to reject such a request, but no T24 response was observed; confirm the actual behavior (READ-FR-3).
• Intended use of `SWF_OUT_GET_MT_BATCH`. Confirm whether the flag is a short-lived operator/scheduler trigger or can stay 1 for long periods, and whether a daily 998 run per deposit is the intended cadence (READ-FR-7).
• Actual timer interval. TimerInterval comes from the encrypted configuration; per-tick volumes below use the host's 10-second fallback for illustration only, and the batch override is assumed off.
• Service identity. Calypso_Conector's Program.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_Conector/Calypso_Conector/Program.cs#L16-L20) also starts as NombreServicio.Swf_OUT_Read. If both hosts are deployed on one server they share the configuration node, the execution-state row, the port-state row, and the log name; confirm and correct in the Calypso_Conector review.
